257
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:50,320
See, I was on the phone with her mother, who, by the way, burst into tears and hung

258
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,340
up on me.

259
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:52,860
D -Does that say anything to you?

260
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:54,420
What's a phone?

261
00:15:55,980 --> 00:15:57,040
I'm ready to go.

262
00:15:57,380 --> 00:15:59,400
Look! How did you get here?

263
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:00,780
You drove me.

264
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:03,120
Look, I was on the phone with your mother, okay?

265
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:06,500
She started crying, and then she told me that I was playing some cruel joke on her.

266
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:07,700
And then she hung up on me.

267
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:09,300
What kind of trouble are you in?

268
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:12,500
Um, I -I'll show you the way.

269
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:16,940
To where? To where I've been trying to go for 17 years.

270
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:20,070
Huh? Ladies and gentlemen...

271
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,940
Now, coming up soon for youngsters out there...

272
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:28,200
Our little friend from Italy, Toppo Giggio.

273
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:31,940
But first, right here on this stage...

274
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:34,940
Paradise Diner is proud to present...

275
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:39,120
Mr. Jimi Hendrix and Liberace, Jimi Lee Giddyup.

276
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:50,880
That's her. Well, Jimmy, it's magic time.

277
00:16:52,700 --> 00:16:54,100
Yeah, I'm with you, Lee.

278
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:15,620
Let's go. Hey, it looked like you floated to me.

279
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,620
We're almost there.

280
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:21,160
I don't see any houses.

281
00:17:22,080 --> 00:17:23,100
Mike, stop the car.

282
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:25,780
Why? Because I'm home.

283
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:27,560
I'm finally home.

284
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:34,500
Tara, we're in the middle of nowhere.

285
00:17:35,980 --> 00:17:36,960
Dance with me, Frankie.

286
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:39,380
It's Mike, remember?

287
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:49,040
Please. Uh, Carol, you're losing me here.

288
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:51,900
For one moment, that's all I ask.

289
00:18:13,380 --> 00:18:16,160
I know we promised to love only each other,

290
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:18,960
but I release you from that promise.

291
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:24,980
I hope you find love.

292
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:26,920
I hope you find happiness.

293
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:31,000
You know, Kara, I just really hope that you're OK.

294
00:18:32,180 --> 00:18:33,620
I miss you.

295
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:37,260
What do you mean?

296
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,080
I know you'll find another love.

297
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:47,440
Look, um, Kara, look, I've got an idea, OK?

298
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:48,940
What do you say you just give me another chance?

299
00:18:48,940 --> 00:18:51,440
I'll drive you home and everything's gonna be okay.

300
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:54,000
All right? Um, come on.

301
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:57,160
Obviously, you've been through a lot of shock today, and you're a little confused.

302
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:59,820
Goodbye! Wait. Hey, where you going?

303
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:02,240
Home! No, home!

304
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:04,540
Kara, look, there's no houses up there!

305
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:06,680
Come on, there's no houses for miles!

306
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:11,500
Kara! Kara! Kara!

307
00:19:12,460 --> 00:19:14,140
Hey, Kara, this isn't funny!

308
00:19:14,140 --> 00:19:17,880
I'll be so lost.

309
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:22,860
Kara! Kara! The time and place.

310
00:19:22,860 --> 00:19:25,440
Kara! I'll be so lost.

311
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:33,420
Kara! Hold my hand and we'll have you there.

312
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:40,920
Hold my hand and I'll take you there.

313
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:51,180
Someone... Someone...

314
00:19:56,520 --> 00:19:59,040
Someone... Honey, are you okay?

315
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:06,920
Yeah. You know, it's just that the one thing that makes no sense whatsoever is...

316
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:11,480
Is... How you guys can be so gullible!

317
00:20:13,060 --> 00:20:15,380
What? None of this happens?

318
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:17,840
Nope. Mike, you scared us to death!

319
00:20:18,060 --> 00:20:19,800
And is there a better night for it?

320
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:22,860
Yeah, you should have made a great pilgrim.

321
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:25,620
Well, you planned all this.

322
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:26,340
No, I didn't.

323
00:20:26,460 --> 00:20:28,300
I just planned to come home and scare Ben.

324
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:30,920
When I knew that he would be here toilet paper in the house.

325
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:32,940
I've had it.

326
00:20:33,820 --> 00:20:37,020
Everybody's accusing me of this, But there's not one scrap of evidence.

327
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,120
How about your hundred pounds of two -ply?

328
00:20:42,100 --> 00:20:43,300
I'll go to my room.

329
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:46,720
You know, you guys being here only made it better.

330
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,480
Thank goodness for this storm.

331
00:20:49,020 --> 00:20:50,540
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

332
00:20:50,940 --> 00:20:52,160
Hey, the storm!

333
00:20:52,240 --> 00:20:54,240
It's over. So I can go?

334
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:55,420
Yeah, go on.

335
00:20:55,860 --> 00:20:57,820
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

336
00:20:58,080 --> 00:21:00,160
Let's go, let's go, Hornbities!

337
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:02,220
Come on, Chrissy, wait for me!

338
00:21:02,700 --> 00:21:04,400
You didn't have me fooled for a second.

339
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:05,800
Oh, come on, Debi.

340
00:21:05,820 --> 00:21:08,580
Can you sit there in damp shorts and tell me that?

341
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:11,400
Huh! Oh, great.

342
00:21:11,500 --> 00:21:13,960
So everybody's happy now, except good old Carol.

343
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:20,940
Yep. Oh, that better be that clown, or else...

344
00:21:20,940 --> 00:21:23,900
Hello. I'm Carol, Louia's friend.

345
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:25,280
This is my brother, my father.

346
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:30,820
Let's go. Did I ever tell you about the Halloween night I had when I was about your

347
00:21:30,820 --> 00:21:31,760
age? Yeah, yeah, yeah.

348
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:32,640
With the yellow eyes?

349
00:21:33,380 --> 00:21:35,220
No, these are orange eyes.

350
00:21:35,820 --> 00:21:37,020
But that's getting ahead of the story.

351
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:39,360
No, this was a Halloween night, much like this.

352
00:21:39,460 --> 00:21:40,440
I was about your age.

353
00:21:41,580 --> 00:21:43,500
And... Oh, I don't have any candy.

354
00:21:43,580 --> 00:21:44,640
I gotta give them fruit.

355
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:46,660
Oh, come on, Dad, don't give them fruit.

356
00:21:46,780 --> 00:21:47,760
What else do I have?

357
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:48,860
Will you give them some money?

358
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:50,760
Yeah, or I could give them one of my kidneys.

359
00:21:54,520 --> 00:21:56,840
Hi, I'm Larry Leakey, Luan's friend.

360
00:21:56,900 --> 00:21:57,860
I'm here to pick up...

361
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:03,080
Uh... Carol, Siever.

362
00:22:04,300 --> 00:22:05,460
Your date? Yes.

363
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,340
Then who'd she leave with?

364
00:22:11,540 --> 00:22:14,940
I hope the wind didn't exaggerate too much about me.

365
00:22:16,560 --> 00:22:18,740
So, what line of work are you in?

366
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:25,020
Procurement. Where are we going?

367
00:22:30,660 --> 00:22:34,520
Happy Halloween from Growing Pays!

368
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:06,960
It's Halloween It's Halloween

369
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:12,100
Breaking your nightmares to love
